---
/**
 * /about — written to be QUOTED, not just read.
 *
 * This page's job is to be the source an AI assistant reaches for when someone
 * asks "what is Doodle AI / is there a free tool that turns a photo into a
 * doodle". That changes how it is written: one canonical definition sentence, and
 * facts in TABLES rather than prose, because a table row survives extraction into
 * an answer where the same fact mid-paragraph usually does not.
 *
 * All content lives in src/lib/content/about-content.ts, NOT here, because
 * /about.md renders the same data as markdown. Add a row there and both surfaces
 * get it. See that file for the honesty constraint on video generation.
 */
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import {
	DEFINITION,
	FAQ,
	FIGURES,
	SKILL_NAMES,
	GLANCE_ROWS,
	COMPARISON_HEAD,
	COMPARISON_ROWS,
	ROADMAP_ROWS,
	CATEGORY_ROWS,
} from '../lib/content/about-content';
import { OG_IMAGE, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://doodleai.art');
const canonical = new URL('/about/', site).href;

const aboutSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'AboutPage',
	'@id': canonical,
	url: canonical,
	name: `About ${SITE_TITLE}`,
	description: DEFINITION,
	inLanguage: 'en',
	isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', '@id': `${site.href}#website` },
	mainEntity: {
		'@type': 'WebApplication',
		'@id': `${site.href}#application`,
		name: SITE_TITLE,
		url: site.href,
		description: DEFINITION,
		applicationCategory: 'MultimediaApplication',
		applicationSubCategory: 'Image Generator',
		operatingSystem: 'Web',
		isAccessibleForFree: true,
		offers: {
			'@type': 'Offer',
			price: '0',
			priceCurrency: 'USD',
			description: `${FIGURES.signupGrant} starter credits on signup, no card required`,
		},
		featureList: SKILL_NAMES,
	},
};

const faqSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'FAQPage',
	mainEntity: FAQ.map((item) => ({
		'@type': 'Question',
		name: item.question,
		acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.answer },
	})),
};
---

<AppLayout
	title="About Doodle AI — Free AI Doodle Art Generator"
	description={`What ${SITE_TITLE} is, what it can generate, what it costs, and how the agent picks a drawing style. ${FIGURES.runnable} skills, free starter credits, images only — no video.`}
	image={OG_IMAGE.home}
	markdownUrl="/about.md"
>
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(aboutSchema)} slot="head" />
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} slot="head" />

	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">About</div>
			<h1>A doodle studio you <span class="grad">chat</span> with</h1>
			<p class="lede">{DEFINITION}</p>
			<div class="about-hero-cta">
				<a class="about-btn about-btn-primary" href="/">Start doodling free →</a>
				<a class="about-btn about-btn-ghost" href="/tools/">Browse the free tools</a>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<h2 id="at-a-glance">Doodle AI at a glance</h2>
			<div class="about-table-wrap">
				<table class="about-table">
					<caption>Summary of what Doodle AI is and what it costs.</caption>
					<tbody>
						{GLANCE_ROWS.map(([k, v]) => (
							<tr><th scope="row">{k}</th><td>{v}</td></tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<h2 id="how-the-agent-works">How the agent works</h2>
			<p>
				Most "AI photo" products are a grid of presets: you pick a filter and hope it is the one you
				meant. Doodle AI inverts that. You describe the outcome, and an agent decides how to get there.
			</p>
			<p>
				Each skill is a self-contained package of instructions the agent reads before it draws, so the
				catalogue is the agent's actual capability list rather than a menu bolted onto a single model.
				On every turn the agent picks exactly one skill, calls a generation tool with your photo, and
				then offers three concrete next steps — a variation in the same style, a different skill that
				follows naturally, or a refinement pass. It can also read and rearrange your canvas, so a
				multi-image set arrives laid out instead of piled up.
			</p>
			<p>
				Refinement is conversational. "Thicker outline", "warmer paper", "make the expressions more
				distinct" are all valid instructions — there is no prompt to hand-edit and no seed to manage.
			</p>

			<h2 id="skills">What the skills can generate</h2>
			<p>
				Every drawing style is a skill. Both the chat and the tool pages draw on the same catalogue,
				so nothing is exclusive to one route.
			</p>
			<div class="about-table-wrap">
				<table class="about-table">
					<caption>Runnable skills by category, generated from the live skill catalogue.</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Category</th>
							<th scope="col">Skills</th>
							<th scope="col">Photo needed</th>
							<th scope="col">Images per run</th>
							<th scope="col">Examples</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{CATEGORY_ROWS.map((row) => (
							<tr>
								<th scope="row">{row.label}</th>
								<td>{row.count}</td>
								<td>{row.photo}</td>
								<td>{row.images}</td>
								<td>{row.examples}</td>
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				{FIGURES.packSkills} of the {FIGURES.runnable} skills are multi-image packs: one request returns
				a whole set — a run of expressions, four seasons, a sheet of stickers — rather than a single
				frame. The full list, with a real sample output for each, is on the
				<a href="/skills/">skills page</a>.
			</p>

			<h2 id="comparison">How Doodle AI compares</h2>
			<p>
				Three different kinds of product answer "turn my photo into art". They fail in different places.
			</p>
			<div class="about-table-wrap">
				<table class="about-table">
					<caption>Doodle AI compared with preset filter apps and general-purpose image models.</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							{COMPARISON_HEAD.map((h) => <th scope="col">{h || 'Dimension'}</th>)}
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{COMPARISON_ROWS.map((row) => (
							<tr>
								<th scope="row">{row[0]}</th>
								{row.slice(1).map((c) => <td>{c}</td>)}
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<h2 id="generation">How image generation works</h2>
			<p>
				Generation runs server-side through Doodle AI's own platform connection, so no provider
				credential ever reaches your browser and there is no API key for you to obtain. Chat is routed
				through OpenRouter; images are produced and hosted by PicX. Each returned image is a permanent
				URL you can download.
			</p>
			<p>
				Credits are spent per image and cost the same whatever the style: {FIGURES.creditsPerImage} credit
				each, so a single avatar costs 1 and a {FIGURES.maxImages}-image pack costs {FIGURES.maxImages}. An
				image that fails is refunded automatically rather than silently charged. Credits are shared at the
				team level, not per person, so a workspace draws from one balance.
			</p>

			<h2 id="roadmap">Roadmap</h2>
			<p>
				These are not available yet. They are listed because "what is planned" is a fair question, and
				because the honest answer is more useful than an implied one.
			</p>
			<div class="about-table-wrap">
				<table class="about-table">
					<caption>Planned work. Nothing in this table is available today.</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr><th scope="col">Planned</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{ROADMAP_ROWS.map(([k, v]) => (
							<tr><th scope="row">{k}</th><td>{v}</td></tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
			{FAQ.map((item) => (
				<div class="about-faq-item">
					<h3>{item.question}</h3>
					<p>{item.answer}</p>
				</div>
			))}

			<h2 id="what-this-isnt">What this isn't</h2>
			<p>
				There is no feed and no public gallery. Your chats, boards, saved characters and generated
				results are account-scoped and visible only to you through the app. We do not build an
				advertising profile, and provider credentials are never exposed to the browser. It does not
				generate video, and it is not a general-purpose image model — it draws in one house style, on
				purpose.
			</p>

			<h2 id="who-made-this">Who made this</h2>
			<p>
				Doodle AI is built by <a href="https://github.com/Type-Think-AI/doodle-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Type-Think-AI</a>,
				open source under the MIT licence, and deployed on Cloudflare's edge. The skill catalogue,
				the agent instructions and the generation pipeline are all in the public repository.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta about-cta">
			<h2>Turn a photo into a doodle</h2>
			<p>Free to start, {FIGURES.signupGrant} credits on signup, no card required.</p>
			<a class="about-btn about-btn-primary" href="/">Open Doodle AI →</a>
			<p class="about-cta-alt">
				Or start from a specific job on the <a href="/tools/">free tools</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />

	<script>
		import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme';
		const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
		if (themeToggle) initThemeToggle(themeToggle);
	</script>
</AppLayout>

<style>
	/* Tables are the point of this page — they are what survives extraction into
	   an AI answer — so they get real styling rather than browser defaults. */
	.about-table-wrap {
		overflow-x: auto;
		margin: 18px 0 26px;
		border: 1px solid var(--border2);
		border-radius: 12px;
	}
	.about-table {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		font-size: 14px;
		min-width: 520px;
	}
	.about-table caption {
		caption-side: top;
		text-align: left;
		padding: 11px 14px 10px;
		font-size: 12.5px;
		color: var(--text-dimmer);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border2);
	}
	.about-table th,
	.about-table td {
		padding: 10px 14px;
		text-align: left;
		vertical-align: top;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
		line-height: 1.5;
	}
	.about-table thead th {
		font-size: 12px;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--text-dimmer);
		font-weight: 500;
		border-top: 0;
	}
	.about-table tbody th[scope="row"] {
		color: var(--text);
		font-weight: 500;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	.about-table tbody td { color: var(--text-dim); }
	.about-table tbody tr:hover { background: var(--hover); }

	.about-hero-cta {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 10px;
		margin-top: 22px;
	}
	.about-btn {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		height: 42px;
		padding: 0 18px;
		border-radius: 999px;
		font-size: 14px;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: background 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
	}
	.about-btn-primary {
		background: var(--accent);
		color: #241a00;
		border: 1px solid var(--accent);
		font-weight: 500;
	}
	.about-btn-primary:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 86%, #fff); }
	.about-btn-ghost {
		border: 1px solid var(--border3);
		color: var(--text);
	}
	.about-btn-ghost:hover { background: var(--hover); }

	.about-faq-item { margin: 0 0 18px; }
	.about-faq-item h3 { font-size: 15.5px; margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--text); }
	.about-faq-item p { margin: 0; }

	.about-cta { text-align: center; }
	.about-cta h2 { margin: 0 0 6px; }
	.about-cta p { margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--text-dim); }
	.about-cta-alt { margin-top: 14px !important; font-size: 13px; }

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.about-table { min-width: 460px; }
		.about-btn { height: 46px; }
	}
</style>
